hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22858","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Sulayman Abu ar-Rabi, from al-Qasim, the freedman of Muawiyah, who said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw people gathered and an old man narrating to them. I said: Who is this? They said: This is Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. So I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever eats meat, let him perform ablution."
